ention  they are playing dodgeball  it's a bold strategy cotton let's see if  it pays off for them having come to the  realization that the bomber effectively  forced them all to engage in an 8-v  a dodgeball match for all the marbles  i'm inclined to say that despite all the  bad things i will no doubt say about him  later  he is for the duration of this fantastic  sports game  the greatest villain in all of fiction  for facilitating this  but all is not as it seems in this crazy  world of hunter hunter dodgeball because  the rules are slightly different and i  wasn't prepared to have  all of patches of houlihan's rules  thrown out in favor of some brand new  ones but  i quickly found my footing here and all  jokes aside this dodgeball game is one  of the most shonen performances i think  this arcane maybe even this series has  ever done and  i'm here for it right off the bat  takashi does a great job with  establishing razer as both dominant and  ruthless whenever we get characters that  are designed like this  with that sort of face juxtaposing them  with some vile actions like killing  someone while smiling is  always effective and unsettling between  the two teams it's clear who we're  rooting for  and systematically we feel the tension  rise as one after another  guns team falters and loses member after  member  [Music]  population you bro this dodgeball match  absolutely  raises guns standing among the rest of  the cast where the others like biscuit  and kilauea were willing to concede or  take a dirty victory  gone straight up refuses to accept  anything other than an absolute  dominant performance in victory his  tenacity his decisiveness his leadership  and his toughness are all on full  display here despite being outmatched  and knocked out once before  not only is he willing and determined  but he's confident in his own power and  ability and  he's got a plan and while killer and  hisoka are apprehensive at first  they backed this little spiky-haired kid