d if you die  well it's even crazier because he gets  up and gets a free turn to try and  finish off his enemy it's a real  testament to the game's accessibility  and breadth of content this month alone  raids released 11 new champions 200 new  missions with legendary champion rewards  and what's more is they've added five  new levels to almost every single one of  the dungeons in the game that's an  incredible amount to add in just one  month  it's a bunch of fun so if it sounds like  it's up your alley make sure to use my  link down below so you can summon some  of the awesome champions i've just  mentioned  just click the link in the description  and i will see you in game  [Music]  i do not like how immediately after the  epic dodgeball match with someone  directly tied to the main goal of the  story the stakes immediately  plummet and shrink as we go back to  playing the game again  and let me make something perfectly  clear i am totally on board with wanting  to like this game i really am  but when we switch from what was once  awesome to now going back to  dual disc card collecting things i can't  help but  feel a little deflated and unfortunately  for the villain i didn't find him to be  entertaining  either we don't know much of anything  about him and he isn't really all that  impressive  he did one thing in the entire story  that i thought was noteworthy and  since then has done little else apart  from wait for the plot to come back  around to him whenever it gets off of  something  unfortunately more interesting with that  said however there's a decent effort on  behalf of tagashi to establish these  bombers as  the villains of this game by contrasting  them heavily with gon kilauea's  playstyle  while they are on top of the world  riding high with almost all of the cards  the feud that they are missing highlight  the difference and establish them as the  villains of this story  in storytelling contrast is one of the  most important elements or tools in 